But wait — is it really a single read? `*desc = READ_ONCE(ring->desc[idx])` — the struct copy compiles to a memcpy-like sequence of loads from the ring into the stack local. There's no bounds-check-then-reread; validation happens after the copy on the local copy. The use in the caller (xsk_generic_xmit uses `desc.len`, `desc.addr` from the stack local). So this snapshot implements the safe pattern already. Interesting — this looks like the fixed upstream code (READ_ONCE was added to xskq_validate_addr in commit 37b076933ca8 "xsk: fix potential double-buffer free in UMEM..."). Actually the fixes: `c497176fb2ee6b3d82b58f4e34bc647e6812a914`? Let me recall — in 4.19, upstream had:

```c
